<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Muhammad al-Nasir</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as al-Nasir fled</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Muhammad al-Nasir was <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/almohad-caliphate">Almohad</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliph</a> from 1199 to 1213, son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yaqub-al-mansur">Yaqub al-Mansur</a>. He faced a coalition of Christian Iberian kingdoms and was decisively defeated at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-las-navas-de-tolosa">Battle of Las Navas de Tolosa</a> in 1212, after which he fled. The defeat marked the beginning of the end of Almohad power in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-andalus">al-Andalus</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/muhammad-al-nasir.jpg" alt="Muhammad al-Nasir" width="320" height="153" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: User:LouisAragon (uploads) · CC BY-SA 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gold_coin_of_Almohad_ruler_Abu_%27Abd_Allah_Muhammad_(r._1199-1213).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
